Third-party material
--------------------

No third-party source code is vendored, copied, generated from or linked into these assemblies. The PDF
object model, the lexer, the object parser, the stream filters (FlateDecode, ASCIIHexDecode and
ASCII85Decode, with the PNG and TIFF predictors), the cross-reference tables, the cross-reference and
object streams, the page tree walk, the object copier and the writer are all written in this repository,
against ISO 32000-1 and ISO 32000-2 as specifications rather than against an implementation.

The only third-party code a consumer receives comes from NuGet, transitively, and only through
SharpCorePDF.DependencyInjection. SharpCorePDF.Domain, SharpCorePDF.Application and
SharpCorePDF.Infrastructure have no package reference at all; SharpCorePDF itself has no code of its own.

    Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder         MIT   Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors
    Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions   MIT
    Microsoft.Extensions.Options                      MIT

Their licence texts travel inside their own packages; nothing of theirs is modified or republished here.
Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers is a development-time dependency only (PrivateAssets="all") and
is not part of any package.

Test fixtures are documents, not code. The ones under tests/ are produced by docs/tools/make-fixtures.py,
which is part of this repository; the encrypted fixtures were additionally produced with pikepdf so that an
independent implementation wrote them. No code from pikepdf, qpdf or any other tool is included, linked or
redistributed, and the generated files carry no attribution requirement. pyHanko, qpdf, pikepdf and pypdf
appear in docs/measurements.md as independent readers that were run against output; they are tools used to
verify, not dependencies.

